; C4 variant vec (RSpice-authored; corpus design C4): the SAR register
; (net/sar8.v) clocked and started by an HSPICE digital vector file, and its
; code checked on b7..b0. The format is HSPICE's (Reference Manual: Commands
; and Control Options, chapter 4 "Digital Vector File Commands"; User Guide:
; Basic Simulation and Analysis, chapter 10, "Specifying a Digital Vector
; File and Mixed Mode Stimuli").
;
; One row every 50 ns. clk is 0 on even rows and 1 on odd ones, so it rises
; from 50 ns + m 100 ns and crosses the register's 0.9 V A/D threshold 0.5 ns
; later; start is high on the first two rows of every microsecond, around
; clock 0 of conversion k at k us + 50 ns, and low on the others. Conversion k
; raises eoc on clock 9, the row at k us + 950 ns, which also gives the code
; it must end with, S_k (net/vin_codes.cir); every other row's outputs are X.
; ODELAY 25 checks it 25 ns later, while the bits hold until the next
; conversion's clock 0.
radix 1 1 4 4
io i i o o
vname clk start b[7:0]
tunit ns
vih 1.8
vil 0
trise 1
tfall 1
voh 1.62
vol 0.18
odelay 25
